Now that we have been able to regroup and redeploy, and we know the location of the Chinese base, we have an opportunity to launch a surprise assault on them. However, the Chinese seem to be jamming our satellites, so we must place nav beacons by hand. One operative will be sent in close to the base to place beacons for the bomber wing that will carry out the strike.

ENGINEERING REPORT:
We have pushed the Red Devil unit into production ahead of schedule, since our existing Razors have developed various problems resulting from their age and the conditions here on Ganymede - where possible, Recyclers have been tooled to build the Red Devil instead of the Razor. Standing Razor units will remain in service, but will be overhauled in rotation.